# Next.js Web Conventions

## Route groups

- `(auth)/` — public: login, register
- `(dashboard)/` — protected: overview, chat, settings, members
- `middleware.ts` — JWT / session route protection

## Data access

- Prefer Server Components fetching `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`
- Pass auth via httpOnly cookies or Authorization header (match auth implementation)
- SSE chat: `EventSource` or `hooks/useChat.ts` for `/ai/conversations/:id/stream`

## Components

- `components/chat/` — ChatWindow, MessageBubble, InputBar
- `components/billing/` — PricingTable, UsageBar, PlanBadge
- `components/shared/` — Sidebar, Avatar, ThemeToggle
- Use `@repo/ui` for shadcn primitives

## Hooks

- `useOrganization`, `useSubscription`, `useChat` — colocate in `hooks/`

## Do not

- Put business rules or plan limits in the frontend only — API enforces limits
- Hardcode API URLs — use `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`
